From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chrisohearn <137103567+chrisohearn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:13:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple: qualify the K114s for suspend-to-idle over the
 adopted N1 link

The adopted link's suspend check admits the J716c and the K114c. On a
K114s (MacBook Pro 14-inch OLED, M5 Pro, Mac17,13) with the N1 described
on port 0, every suspend-to-idle is therefore refused with -EBUSY from
the host's noirq suspend.

The K114s has the same T6050 host as the K114c and the K116s, the N1 on
the port the boot loader trains, and in the macOS 27.2 (26B8125) Apple
device trees its PCIe nodes are identical to the K116s's. It describes no
second, kernel-trained port, so every device below the host must still be
in D0, as on the J716c and the K114c. Let it through the same checks.

This is the K114s-only half of sleep-lid/0001 to 0003 of r3a, cut to
apply on the shared kernel series without the K116s changes (aurora-silicon/linux
pull request 1647), which a K114s with no second port does not need.

Compile-tested only (pcie-apple.o, clang 23, no warnings). Not yet run
through a suspend on a K114s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index b6c3b98af2..b28b9d1f4b 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -5819,9 +5819,16 @@ static int apple_pcie_check_adopted_s2idle(struct apple_pcie *pcie)
 	struct apple_pcie_port *port;
 	int error = 0;
 
-	/* Other adopted platforms and deeper sleep remain unqualified. */
+	/*
+	 * Qualified on the J716c, the K114c and the K114s. The K114s is the
+	 * K114c's M5 Pro sibling: the same PCIe host and the N1 on the
+	 * loader-trained port 0, and no second port. It takes the same checks; it
+	 * has not been through a suspend on the hardware yet. Other adopted
+	 * platforms and deeper sleep remain unqualified.
+	 */
 	if (!(of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j716c") ||
-	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k114c")) || !pm_suspend_no_platform())
+	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k114c") ||
+	      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,k114s")) || !pm_suspend_no_platform())
 		return -EBUSY;
 
 	if (!(readl(pcie->base + CORE_RC_CTL) & CORE_RC_CTL_RUN) ||
